  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-07-25T22:20:06.079Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "**Issue:**\nWhen upgrading a project from SDK2, I get these errors in my console, and the VRCSDK Menu is mostly empty.\n**Errors:**\n```\nAssets/VRCSDK/Dependencies/VRChat/Scripts/Validation/AvatarValidation.cs(162,13): error CS0246: The type or namespace name 'VRC_SpatialAudioSource' could not be found (are you missing a using directive or an assembly reference?)\nAssets/VRCSDK/Dependencies/VRChat/Scripts/Validation/AvatarValidation.cs(162,97): error CS0246: The type or namespace name 'VRC_SpatialAudioSource' could not be found (are you missing a using directive or an assembly reference?)\nAssets/VRCSDK/Dependencies/VRChat/Scripts/Validation/AvatarValidation.cs(167,78): error CS0246: The type or namespace name 'VRC_SpatialAudioSource' could not be found (are you missing a using directive or an assembly reference?)\n```\n**Upgrade process:**\n1. Quit Unity\n2. Delete old SDK\n3. Open project\n4. Import new SDK\n**SDK:**\nVRCSDK3-AVATAR-2020.07.23.21.16_Public\n\n**Workarounds/fixes tried:**\n• Deleting/rebuilding the Library folder.\n\n** Fixed by:**\nRemoving SDK2 references from `Scripting Define Symbols` under `Project Settings/Player`.",
